# Goal, result and feedback, each with bounded sequences and its own constants.
#
# Constants live in a separate module per section in the generated crate. The
# stronger case -- the *same* constant name in two sections, as newer nav2
# actions have -- cannot be expressed through rosidl_generate_interfaces: the
# upstream C and C++ generators emit one enum per action and fail with
# "redeclaration of enumerator" before the Rust generator sees the definition.
# That case is covered by the action template's unit tests instead.

geometry_msgs/Point[<=4] waypoints
string label
---
uint8 RESULT_NONE=0
uint8 RESULT_SUCCEEDED=1
bool success
geometry_msgs/Point[<=4] visited
---
uint8 FEEDBACK_NONE=0
uint8 FEEDBACK_RUNNING=1
float32 progress
geometry_msgs/Point[<=4] remaining
